  data: {
    LLM: "1. The player to dealer's left pitches the first card; its suit becomes trump. 2. The first trick is kept face up with a trump visible on top; later tricks are face down. 3. If a player has no trumps and no counting cards above 9 and is not winning the current trick, they may throw in their hand and take no further part while partner continues. 4. Score points in order High, Low, Jack, Game.",
    Player: "1. The player to dealer's left pitches the first card; its suit becomes trump. 2. The first trick is kept face up with a trump visible on top; later tricks are face down. 3. If a player has no trumps and no counting cards above 9 and is not winning the current trick, they may throw in their hand and take no further part while partner continues. 4. Score points in order High, Low, Jack, Game.",
    objective: 'First team to reach 11 points (or 15 in some leagues) by winning High, Low, Jack, and Game.',
    gameplay: "1. The player to dealer's left pitches the first card; its suit becomes trump. 2. The first trick is kept face up with a trump visible on top; later tricks are face down. 3. If a player has no trumps and no counting cards above 9 and is not winning the current trick, they may throw in their hand and take no further part while partner continues. 4. Score points in order High, Low, Jack, Game.",
    keyRules: [
      'High (1 pt): Team dealt the highest trump.',
      'Low (1 pt): Team dealt the lowest trump (unlike Lancashire, this is awarded to the holder).',
      'Jack (1 pt): Winning the trick containing the Jack of trumps.',
      'Game (1 pt): Higher pip total (A=4, K=3, Q=2, J=1, 10=10).',
      "Pitcher's partner must keep their cards face down until the Pitch is made.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
